.\" SPDX-License-Identifier: LGPL-3.0-or-later
.Dd November 20, 2026
.Dt NOQTIS-SMIME 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm noqtis-smime
.Nd sign, verify, encrypt or decrypt mail (S/MIME, CMS)
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm noqtis smime
.Cm sign
.Fl k Ar key
.Fl -cert Ar cert
.Op Fl -detached
.Op Fl -der | Fl -text | Fl -entity
.Op Fl o Ar out
.Op Fl f | Fl -force
.Op Fl -pass-fd Ar n | Fl -pass-env Ar name
.Ar file
.Nm noqtis smime
.Cm verify
.Fl -anchor Ar cert
.Op Fl -anchor Ar cert ...
.Op Fl -content Ar file
.Op Fl -entity
.Op Fl o Ar out
.Op Fl f | Fl -force
.Ar file
.Nm noqtis smime
.Cm encrypt
.Fl -to Ar cert
.Op Fl -to Ar cert ...
.Op Fl -der | Fl -text | Fl -entity
.Op Fl o Ar out
.Op Fl f | Fl -force
.Ar file
.Nm noqtis smime
.Cm decrypt
.Fl k Ar key
.Op Fl -cert Ar cert
.Op Fl -entity
.Op Fl o Ar out
.Op Fl f | Fl -force
.Op Fl -pass-fd Ar n | Fl -pass-env Ar name
.Ar file
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm noqtis smime
writes and reads S/MIME messages (RFC 8551), the signed and encrypted
mail of the Cryptographic Message Syntax (RFC 5652), with the
certificates
.Xr noqtis-cert 1
makes.
.Bl -tag -width "encrypt"
.It Cm sign
Sign
.Ar file
with the secret signature key
.Ar key ,
whose certificate is
.Fl -cert Ar cert :
ML-DSA (RFC 9882), SLH-DSA (RFC 9814) or Ed25519 (RFC 8419).
The message carries the certificate.
With
.Fl -detached
the content stays in the clear beside the signature
.Pq multipart/signed ,
so that a reader without S/MIME still shows it; otherwise it is inside
.Pq application/pkcs7-mime .
.It Cm verify
Check a signed message against the trust anchors given with
.Fl -anchor
(up to 32 certificates, PEM or DER): the signer's certificate is one of
them, or chains to one.
It prints who signed, as in EXAMPLES, with the first 16 hex digits of
the SHA-256 of the signer's certificate,
on standard output, or on standard error when
.Fl o
is
.Ar - ;
with
.Fl o
it writes the content.
A signature that does not verify prints a line with
.Ql FAILED
on standard output.
The certificates must be valid at the signing time the message states.
The certificate\(aqs validity is judged at the message\(aqs signing time when it carries one, and that time is the signer\(aqs claim unless a timestamp covers it.
.It Cm encrypt
Encrypt
.Ar file
to the ML-KEM certificates given with
.Fl -to
(up to 32): AES-256-GCM, the content key carried to each recipient by
ML-KEM (RFC 9629, RFC 9936).
Encryption does not say who sent a message: to do both, sign first and
encrypt the result.
.It Cm decrypt
Open an encrypted message with the ML-KEM secret key
.Ar key ;
.Fl -cert
names that key's certificate, and so its entry among the recipients;
without it, the key is tried on each recipient's entry in turn.
.El
.Pp
The options:
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl -der
Write the CMS structure itself, in DER, in place of a MIME message;
not with
.Fl -text
or
.Fl -entity .
.Cm verify
and
.Cm decrypt
read either form;
.Cm verify
takes what a detached DER signature signs with
.Fl -content Ar file .
.It Fl -text
The content is text: it is carried as it is
.Pq text/plain ,
readable in a detached message, and its line ends become CRLF as S/MIME
requires.
Without it the content is carried in base64 and every byte comes back
as it was.
.It Fl -entity
.Ar file
is a MIME entity already, header and body;
.Cm verify
and
.Cm decrypt
then write the entity instead of its body.
.It Fl o Ar out , Fl -out Ns = Ns Ar out
The output; standard output when it is not given or is
.Ar - .
A file is created with mode 0644 whatever the umask; the plaintext of
.Cm decrypt
is owner-only (mode 0600), as
.Xr noqtis-unbox 1
and
.Xr noqtis-dec 1
write theirs.
.It Fl -pass-fd Ar n , Fl -pass-env Ar name
The passphrase of a protected
.Ar key .
.It Fl f , Fl -force
Replace an existing
.Ar out .
.El
.Pp
The input
.Ar file ,
and the
.Fl -content
of
.Cm verify ,
are read whole, up to 1 GiB; a certificate up to 1 MiB.
.Cm sign
writes as the signing time the current time, or
.Ev SOURCE_DATE_EPOCH
when it is set
.Pq Xr noqtis 1 .
.Sh EXIT STATUS
0 on success;
1 when
.Cm verify
finds that a signature does not verify or its signer is not trusted;
2 on a usage or file error, and when a message does not open.
.Sh EXAMPLES
.Bd -literal
$ noqtis smime sign -k me --cert me.crt --detached --text \e
      -o note.eml note.txt
$ noqtis smime verify --anchor me.crt note.eml
note.eml: OK, signed by Ada Example <ada@example.org> (certificate ...)
$ noqtis smime encrypt --to bob-kem.crt -o secret.p7m report.pdf
$ noqtis smime decrypt -k bob-kem -o report.pdf secret.p7m
.Ed
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr noqtis 1 ,
.Xr noqtis-cert 1 ,
.Xr nqcmssign 3 ,
.Xr nqsmsign 3
